  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, the Government of the United Republic of Tanzania reported on the application of ratified Conventions, meeting its obligation under article 22 of the ILO Constitution and addressing comments and recommendations of the Committee of Experts on the Application of Conventions and Recommendations (CEACR). From May 2022, the ILO, with support from UN Multi Partner Trust Fund, provided assistant to the government to prepare and submit reports on the application of ratified conventions. This was done in consultation with social partners and reflected in the CEACR reports published in 2022 and 2023.</narrative>
   </description>
